The boat arrives at the other side of the water.
The harbour bus stops at a small pier.
I get off the boat.
The trip by boat is now over.
I check the map on my phone.
I am going to a small kiosk.
The kiosk is located over on a corner.
I walk up the street.
I see the shop at the end of the road.
I open the door and walk in.
A young man stands behind the register.
"Hi," he says kindly.
"Hi, I am going to pick up a package," I say.
The man nods and smiles.
He asks for my name.
"My name is Maya," I answer.
He finds a large box on a shelf.
He gives the package to me.
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
Now I take the long trip home again with my package.
